00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:18.920
How it works when the question is who decides the answer starts with a lock, not a vote.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:24.240
In a crypto-settled contract, collateral stays put until an Oracle brings in a result,

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:30.200
and winning claims can be redeemed. An ACM computing surveys paper calls that the Oracle

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:36.400
problem. The contract can see on-chain data, but the real event sits off-chain, so something

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.880
has to carry the outside result onto the chain.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.880
That survey splits the designs in two.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:46.780
Voting-based systems finalize an outcome mainly from what participants have staked.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:52.620
Reputation-based systems mix reputation and performance metrics with authenticity proofs

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.700
meant to support correctness and integrity.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:04:00.280
Both are ways to hand a smart contract a final result, and the paper points to remaining

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:03.500
challenges and later research rather than a finished method.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:07.200
A separate paper on archive looks at the weight itself.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:12.840
If collateral is locked until Oracle Settlement, a near-certain dollar is a delayed dollar.

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:18.420
The price then holds a maturity-dependent settlement discount on top of beliefs about the outcome.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:24.500
The authors build an implied discount curve from persistent near-certain contracts, using

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:29.560
the settlement times that actually occurred, and they summarize it as an annualized settlement

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:29.880
wedge.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:36.240
edge. Those wedges are positive, they change with maturity, and they move through time. Repricing

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:42.840
along those curves cuts the near certainty horizon gradient by roughly 48-88%. The paper

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:48.460
reads much of that raw maturity pattern as priced settlement friction, not forecast error alone.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:54.920
Negris conversion squeezes the discounts by recycling part of a position into synthetic collateral.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:05:00.320
yield bearing collateral flattens the curve because the locked money is less costly to hold.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:06.680
Pricing quality on this account depends on settlement mechanics, how productive the collateral is,

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:13.180
and whether capital can be recycled. A price near certainty is a belief, and it is also a claim on

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:19.200
cash that cannot move until an oracle report, a stake-weighted vote, or a reputation-weighted check

